  23: # Plan: installer transaction implementation (PR 69), test-first
  24: 
  25: Status: ready for owner review, 2026-09-18. Built from a first-hand read of the
  26: design, the review record, all of `bin/install.js` and the acceptance test, plus two
  27: read-only exploration reports and one design critique; every claim the plan leans on
  28: was re-checked directly. Nothing outside this file has been edited. No installer edit
  29: happens before approval.
  30: 
  31: ## Context
  32: 
  33: `bin/install.js` on `chore/upstream-bump-1.9.1` (draft PR 69, head `8c78d21f`, in
  34: sync with origin) snapshots a predicted path list, so a failed install leaves about
  35: 622 files behind while printing `Rollback applied` unconditionally. The owner
  36: accepted a redesign on 2026-09-18 after four review rounds and eleven decisions:
  37: `docs/reviews/installer-rollback-redesign-2026-09-18.md` (the design) and
  38: `docs/reviews/installer-rollback-design-review-2026-09-18.md` (the review record).
  39: Those decisions are fixed. This plan implements the design, RED first.
  40: 
  41: Work happens in the worktree `C:\Projects\get-stuff-done\.claude\worktrees\skin-campaign`
  42: by explicit path (the shell working directory does not persist between calls).
  43: 
  44: ## Invariants throughout (risky flow: destructive filesystem code)
  45: 
  46: - No test, script or manual run ever targets the real `~/.claude`. Every fixture is a
  47:   disposable directory; destructive RED cases aim at copies (mistakes-log Testing 6).
  48: - The installer never opens a file outside its roots (truth 8). Tests assert it.
  49: - A rollback never deletes or overwrites owner bytes in place (truth 3).
  50: - The eleven owner decisions are not reopened. If implementation shows one is unsafe:
  51:   stop, and ask with the evidence inside the AskUserQuestion text.
  52: - Rollback path for this work itself: every step is its own commit on the PR branch;
  53:   `git revert <sha>` undoes any step. No bare `git stash`. No force-push.
  54: - At most three process-heavy shells; cargo-style concurrency rule applies to test
